<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product basis levels.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product basis levels.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NS-no seller T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount NB-no bidder)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	  MONTH	   PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> August	    40/50 P	August	  60/75 P</p>
<p> Sept	    140/150 P	Sept	  145/160 P</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> August	    22/19 D	August	  21/18 D</p>
<p> Sept		2 D/3 P	Sept	    1 D/1 P</p>
<p> Oct		 15/17 P	Oct	     16/18 P</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> August	   125/160 P	August	130/160 P</p>
<p> Sept	     115/160 P	Sept	  110/160 P</p>
<p> Oct		130/160 P	Oct	   120/150 P</p>
